35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The billing system is inefficient, with one person bearing the initial cost. Also, we're wasting money on supplies; we have duplicates of the same spray and are spending over 2,000 yen monthly.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"A full pass takes over an hour and a half, which is more than I expected. Also, an outside firm requires us to tidy up first, so it doesn't actually remove all the work.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears our definitions of ""clean"" are delightfully subjective; some consider a wiped basin a victory, while others demand a pristine drain. Furthermore, the kitchen burden is quite unevenly distributed among us.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"It's no wonder we're fighting! The house chat is just a loop of people nagging each other. Plus, that bathroom grout is a nightmare—the black spots returned in less than two weeks because of the poor ventilation.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It's worrying to see the chat becoming a place for nagging. I noticed that many of us are away for long stretches, and the previous tenants warned that a rigid split led to them barely speaking by the second year.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, if an outside firm still requires us to tidy up, the cost might not be worth the effort. We should consider if the financial burden is being shared fairly.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Exactly. If we still have to spend time prepping the rooms, we aren't actually buying back our time. We need to be realistic about the total hours required for a proper clean.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, while the finances are a concern, I suspect the real friction stems from the fact that some of us are essentially cleaning up after a handful of chefs while others barely touch a kettle.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, exactly! It's that unpredictability that's the worst. One day it's a palace, the next it's a disaster zone. And don't even get me started on the bathroom—it's a losing battle against the mold!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, it sounds so stressful to feel like you're fighting a losing battle. I'm worried that if we focus too much on the ""disaster zones,"" we might end up blaming each other instead of working together.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, while harmony is important, ignoring the financial imbalance and waste won't solve the tension. We are spending money on duplicates and relying on one person to front the bills. That is a recipe for resentment.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, I agree that financial clarity is necessary, but the time cost is the more invisible burden. If a full pass takes nearly two hours, we can't just ignore the physical labor involved.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are debating whether the primary burden is financial or physical. However, both are secondary to the fact that our standards are inconsistent and our usage is wildly asymmetrical. Logic suggests we cannot fix the ""how"" until we address the ""who.""","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, you're always so logical! But while you're figuring out the ""who,"" I'm the one bracing myself before I even open the bathroom door. We need a system that guarantees a baseline of clean, regardless of who's cooking.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I understand your point about usage, but I'm afraid that focusing too much on ""who"" is responsible might make us feel like we're policing each other. I just want us to stay friends.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Toshio,,Friendship is a luxury we can't afford if the basic logistics are broken. We need a system that automates the payments and the supply list so no one is left out of pocket or buying duplicates.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree that logistics are key, but automation doesn't solve the time drain. If we don't account for the actual hours spent, we'll just be automating a system that still leaves some of us exhausted.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"While I admire the passion for logistics and labor, we are essentially arguing over how to decorate a house that is currently on fire. If we ignore the usage gap, we are simply automating unfairness.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, you're making it sound like a tragedy! But seriously, if we just focus on ""fairness"" and ""usage,"" we'll spend all year arguing. I just want to know that the bathroom isn't a swamp when I wake up!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I think we all just want a peaceful home. If we focus too much on who did what or who spent more, we might end up like the previous tenants. Let's find a way to be kind to each other.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
