59,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is the most logical for consistency, but we must fix the billing. If we use a service, we need a strict, automated way to settle the invoice so one person isn't always fronting the cost.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option B is problematic because the prep work still falls on us. If we have to tidy up before they arrive, we aren't actually eliminating the time drain, just adding a financial cost to it.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is a recipe for stagnation, and Option C merely rotates the unfairness. If we ignore the usage gap, we are simply scheduling our resentment. I find Option B the most tolerable, provided we automate the payments.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"Option B sounds like a dream for my sanity! If a professional handles the bathroom, I can stop playing ""mold roulette"" every morning. As long as we don't spend hours prepping, it's a win.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried that Option A might lead to the same silence the previous tenants experienced. Option C feels a bit rigid, but Option B could be a nice way to take the pressure off us and keep the peace.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, the prep work is a minor inconvenience compared to the current chaos. If we choose Option B, we can establish a shared fund for supplies to stop the duplicate spending and ensure the invoice is split instantly.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, a ""minor inconvenience"" is still time taken from our personal lives. If we spend thirty minutes tidying before a cleaner arrives, we're still managing the labor. I'm concerned Option B is an expensive illusion of freedom.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, your commitment to time-efficiency is admirable, though perhaps a bit optimistic. Whether we spend thirty minutes tidying for a professional or two hours scrubbing a drain ourselves, the latter is far more taxing on the soul.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, you're so dramatic! But you're right—scrubbing a drain is a soul-crushing experience. I'd much rather spend thirty minutes tidying than an hour fighting a losing battle against the bathroom grout.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, I understand your concern about the time, but maybe the trade-off is worth it if it stops us from nagging each other in the chat? I think Option B could really help us focus on being housemates instead of managers.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, exactly. Removing the management role from our friendship is the only way to stop the nagging. If we combine Option B with a transparent, shared account for the invoice and supplies, we eliminate both the emotional and financial friction.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, transparency doesn't reduce the actual hours spent. If we choose Option B, we are paying a premium for a service that still requires our labor to be effective. I'm not convinced it's a rational trade-off.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, your pursuit of a perfectly rational trade-off is a noble, if exhausting, endeavor. However, the current ""free"" system is costing us our peace of mind, which is a currency far more precious than a few thousand yen.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, you're overthinking the minutes! I'd happily trade a few ""inefficient"" minutes of tidying for the guarantee that I won't walk into a disaster zone. Option B is the only one that actually solves the consistency problem.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I agree with May. Even if it's not perfectly efficient, the emotional cost of arguing over the kitchen or bathroom is much higher. Option B seems like the best way to ensure we're still on speaking terms next year.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"I've heard enough. Option B is the only choice that addresses the consistency and the emotional friction. As long as we implement a strict payment system to avoid any one person being out of pocket, I vote for B.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I cannot agree that the trade-off is rational. Option B adds a financial burden without fully removing the time commitment. However, Option C is too rigid and Option A risks stagnation. I'll vote for B, but only as a compromise.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Since we have reached a consensus that the emotional cost of our current arrangement is far too high, I shall join the majority. Option B is the most elegant solution to our collective dysfunction. I vote for B.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I'm so glad we're finally on the same page! No more guessing games or moldy surprises for me. I'm voting for B with a huge smile on my face!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,I'm so relieved we could find a solution that prioritizes our harmony. I really want us to enjoy living together without any lingering resentment. I'll happily vote for B!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
